    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d444">

                <pb facs="0556" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg448"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Señor Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May 3,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Romero</hi>: I beg to state that, as
                    appears by a letter of the War Department of 1st instant, Lieut. Walker, Third
                    Cavalry, has captured Delfino Garcia, one of Maugua de Agua men—a disturber, as
                    understood, of the peace on the border.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
